# SEO Conventions

Metadata defaults, crawler policy, structured data, and social-preview patterns for this template. Semantic HTML, heading order, and alt text live in `ui-accessibility.mdc`. SSR, `next/image`, and metadata API mechanics live in `nextjs.mdc`. Auth boundary and route groups: `AGENTS.md`, `LEXICON.md`.

**Hard constraint (enforced):** never hardcode `http://localhost:3000`, read `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` outside the resolver, or construct `new URL()` with a literal origin — see AGENTS.md § Hard constraints (`check:seo-base-url`). Bare-string absolute canonicals are guidance-only (canonical discipline below).

## Metadata source of truth

- Site-wide defaults: [`src/config/site.ts`](../../src/config/site.ts) (`getSiteMetadata`) — name, title template, description, root Open Graph defaults via `siteOpenGraphBase` (including `siteName` and `type: 'website'`), and `twitter.card: 'summary_large_image'`.
- Root wire-up: [`src/app/layout.tsx`](../../src/app/layout.tsx) calls `getSiteMetadata(getSiteUrl())`.
- Per-page marketing metadata: `getPageMetadata` in [`src/config/site.ts`](../../src/config/site.ts) — sole source of `og:url` on indexable marketing routes; shared copy lives in [`src/app/(marketing)/_lib/page-meta.ts`](../../src/app/(marketing)/_lib/page-meta.ts). Spreads `siteOpenGraphBase` so per-page `openGraph` retains site-level fields.
- **Merge rule:** Next.js replaces nested `openGraph` / `twitter` objects rather than merging fields — any segment that sets its own must spread `siteOpenGraphBase` (and repeat `twitter.card` if it sets `twitter`).
- Other per-page overrides: export `metadata` or `generateMetadata` on the page/layout; inherit the title template from root.

## Base URL

[`src/utils/site-url.ts`](../../src/utils/site-url.ts) is the **only** resolver for `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`, `VERCEL_URL`, and the `http://localhost:3000` dev fallback.

- Absolute URLs (sitemap, robots sitemap ref, JSON-LD, OG metadata base): `getSiteUrl()` or `metadataBase` from root layout.
- Relative canonicals (e.g. `alternates: { canonical: '/' }`) resolve against `metadataBase` — preferred over hardcoded absolute origins.
- External product links (GitHub, docs) may stay bare literals; they are not site-base URLs.

## Per-surface indexing

| Surface | Policy | Layout |
| ------- | ------ | ------ |
| Marketing `(marketing)` | Indexable | Landing page sets canonical |
| Auth `/auth/**` | `noindex` | [`src/app/auth/layout.tsx`](../../src/app/auth/layout.tsx) |
| App `(app)` | `noindex` | [`src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`](../../src/app/(app)/layout.tsx) |
| Admin `/admin/**` | `noindex` | [`src/app/admin/layout.tsx`](../../src/app/admin/layout.tsx) |

Defense-in-depth on top of the auth proxy — a route accidentally made public cannot leak into an index.

## Crawler surface

- **Robots:** [`src/utils/robots-policy.ts`](../../src/utils/robots-policy.ts) + [`src/app/robots.ts`](../../src/app/robots.ts) — retrieval/user-fetch bots allowed; training crawlers **allowed by default** via `ALLOW_TRAINING_CRAWLERS` in the policy file. Spinoffs that want to block training crawlers set the flag to `false`. `/robots.txt` is on the auth-boundary public allowlist so crawlers can fetch the policy without a session.
- **Two crawler classes, one policy flag.** `ALLOW_TRAINING_CRAWLERS` governs *training* crawlers only (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Bytespider, Meta-ExternalAgent, and the Google-Extended / Applebot-Extended robots.txt tokens). *Retrieval* and *user-fetch* bots — OAI-SearchBot, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot, Googlebot, Bingbot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-User, Perplexity-User — stay allowed regardless of the flag. Blocking retrieval bots removes the site from AI answers entirely; blocking training crawlers is a policy choice with no citation cost. Never fold the two classes into one disallow.
- **`llms.txt` is not an SEO surface.** Google Search ignores `llms.txt` and similar AI text files — presence or absence changes nothing for indexing, ranking, or AI-answer retrieval, so neither is a finding here. Whether the template ships one as agent-onboarding infrastructure is a separate question this rule does not decide.
- **Sitemap:** [`src/utils/sitemap-routes.ts`](../../src/utils/sitemap-routes.ts) via [`discoverMarketingRoutes()`](../../src/utils/discover-app-routes.ts) — `(marketing)` routes only; auth/app/admin never listed. `/sitemap.xml` is on the auth-boundary public allowlist so crawlers can fetch it without a session.

## Structured data

[`src/utils/structured-data.ts`](../../src/utils/structured-data.ts) — `Organization` + `WebSite` JSON-LD on the landing page ([`src/app/(marketing)/page.tsx`](../../src/app/(marketing)/page.tsx)). `getOrganizationWebSiteJsonLdScript` returns the escaped script body (`<` → `\u003c`), already serialized; pages inject it directly into `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without stringifying. Extend the helper for new schema types; do not inline JSON-LD on pages.

- **Markup must match visible page content.** Do not mark up facts, questions, or ratings the page does not actually render.
- **Do not add schema types for rich-result eligibility alone.** Add a type because it describes the page. `FAQPage` and `HowTo` rich results are both retired in Google Search — the types remain valid schema.org vocabulary, but neither buys a search appearance. Do not propose them as an SEO win.
- **Structured data is not required for AI search surfaces.** It helps rich-result eligibility; it is not a GEO lever.

## Social preview images

- Shared template: [`src/utils/og-image.tsx`](../../src/utils/og-image.tsx) (`createOgImageResponse`).
- Per-route segment files: `opengraph-image.tsx` (e.g. root + [`src/app/auth/login/opengraph-image.tsx`](../../src/app/auth/login/opengraph-image.tsx)). New public marketing routes add their own segment file; title, description, and `alt` come from the same object in [`page-meta.ts`](../../src/app/(marketing)/_lib/page-meta.ts) (or site config for root).
- OG/twitter image paths bypass auth via [`src/utils/proxy-matcher.ts`](../../src/utils/proxy-matcher.ts) — keep in sync with [`src/proxy.ts`](../../src/proxy.ts). Include `/icon` and nested `*/icon` alongside `/opengraph-image`, `/twitter-image`, and their nested variants. Route-group metadata URLs carry an optional 5–6 character hash suffix (`opengraph-image-959drp`); the matcher permits that suffix only at the image position.

## Favicon

- Shared util: [`src/utils/brand-mark-image.tsx`](../../src/utils/brand-mark-image.tsx) (`createBrandMarkImageResponse`) — primary-filled rounded square + `siteConfig.Logo`.
- Segment file: [`src/app/icon.tsx`](../../src/app/icon.tsx) — re-exports size/contentType and calls the util. No static `favicon.ico`; the dynamic route wins.
- `/icon` and nested `*/icon` bypass auth via [`src/utils/proxy-matcher.ts`](../../src/utils/proxy-matcher.ts) — keep in sync with [`src/proxy.ts`](../../src/proxy.ts). Hashed route-group suffixes follow the same 5–6 character bound as OG/twitter images.

## Satori constraints (OG + favicon)

`ImageResponse` / Satori silently renders blank glyphs on violation — no error. Applies to [`src/utils/og-image.tsx`](../../src/utils/og-image.tsx) and [`src/utils/brand-mark-image.tsx`](../../src/utils/brand-mark-image.tsx):

- **Inline styles only** — no Tailwind classes in the JSX tree.
- **Explicit stroke color** on Lucide icons — never `currentColor`.
- **Explicit `width` / `height` props** on icons — never CSS sizing.
- **`display: 'flex'`** on container divs that wrap children.

`siteConfig.Logo` is typed `LucideIcon` for this reason — see comment on the field in [`src/config/site.ts`](../../src/config/site.ts). Unit tests assert non-blank PNG output (magic bytes + byte-length threshold); `instanceof ImageResponse` alone is insufficient.

## Content standards (guidance)

- **Unique title + description** on every page — auth screens already export per-page titles; follow that pattern.
- **Answer-first structure** — lead with the user's question or need, then detail.
- **No content written for crawlers.** Content chunking, keyword-variant pages, and AI-targeted rewrites are not required by any current engine and read as scaled-content spam. Write for the reader.
- **Canonical discipline** — one self-referential canonical per indexable page; no duplicate indexable URLs; prefer relative paths resolved via `metadataBase`.

## New public page checklist

- [ ] Add a `page-meta.ts` entry and wire `export const metadata = getPageMetadata(...)` on the page
- [ ] Route group correct for indexing (`(marketing)` = indexable; others inherit `noindex` from layout)
- [ ] `opengraph-image.tsx` reading the same page-meta object for title, description, and `alt`
- [ ] Metadata image file lives only under `(marketing)/`, `auth/`, or directly in `src/app/` — anywhere else fails `check:auth-boundary`
- [ ] Sitemap auto-includes new `(marketing)` routes via discovery — no manual sitemap edit unless discovery rules change
- [ ] JSON-LD only at landing level unless extending `structured-data.ts` for a new schema type

